From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:29:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add ggl-svc, a service manager for builds without systemd

ggl-svcd runs the core daemons and the units ggdeploymentd generates for
components. It implements the subset of systemd unit semantics they use
(Type, ExecStart, User, Group, WorkingDirectory, Environment, Restart,
RestartSec, RemainAfterExit, SuccessExitStatus, StartLimitBurst and
After/Wants/BindsTo ordering), forwards unit output to syslog, and
exposes unit state over a Unix socket. Readiness of the core daemons is
the appearance of their core-bus socket (X-GGL-ReadySocket), in place of
socket activation. Requests that change state are accepted from root
only.

A systemctl front end forwards the commands ggdeploymentd issues (link,
enable, disable, start, stop, restart, daemon-reload, reset-failed,
reboot).

gghealthd gets a matching backend: lifecycle states, restarts,
systemd-notify style state updates and lifecycle subscriptions come from
ggl-svcd instead of systemd's D-Bus API, with the same state mapping.

ggipc-auth asks ggl-svcd which unit an IPC peer belongs to (the unit
whose main process is the peer or one of its ancestors), in place of
systemd's cgroup-based sd_pid_get_unit(), and derives the component name
from it exactly as before.

Only built with GGL_PORTABLE_CORE=ON.

Signed-off-by: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Upstream: not yet submitted (developed on the esp32s31/v2.7.0 branch of a fork)
